From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winex11, explorer, windows.ui: Linux programs' progress and badges on their taskbar buttons

A Windows program shows progress on its taskbar button and a badge
(ITaskbarList3 SetProgressValue, SetOverlayIcon: Telegram for Windows'
unread count); a Linux program said the same and nothing showed it
(David 2026-11-27: Linux programs first class). Linux programs say it two
ways:

- XApp's _NET_WM_XAPP_PROGRESS (0-100) and _NET_WM_XAPP_PROGRESS_PULSE on
  their window (Firefox's downloads, file copies). winex11 hears them on a
  framed window (sg_embed.c) and tells its frame, the shell's window.
- com.canonical.Unity.LauncherEntry's Update on the session bus (count,
  progress, urgent: Telegram, Chromium-based programs), which sg-session's
  sg-notify-bridge passes to the Linux notifications host
  (SgLinuxNotifications, 9512) as LAUNCHER <AUMID> count progress urgent;
  the host finds the app's frames -- explorer tags each with its app's ID
  (SgLinuxAppId, a global atom) -- tells them the count and progress, again
  every two seconds for windows opened since, and flashes them while the
  app is urgent.

The frame (explorer's SgLinuxWindow) takes SG_FRAME_PROGRESS (WM_APP +
0x5350: none, indeterminate, normal and a percent) and SG_FRAME_BADGE
(WM_APP + 0x5351: the count) and shows them as ITaskbarList3's progress and
overlay do: the button's fill, and a red badge with the count (99+).

Gate: test/linuxprogress-gate.sh (mutants SG_MUTANT_EMBED_NO_PROGRESS,
SG_MUTANT_FRAME_NO_PROGRESS, SG_MUTANT_LAUNCHER_IGNORED).
